# Project Overview

Read-only PHP dashboard over a MariaDB DAQ / run-log database. Per-run tables
`DAQ_config`, `EPICS_data`, and `Analysis` hang off `Run_info` (`run_number`).
Aggregates live in `Grouped_Analysis` (`group_number`). The live schema is
owned elsewhere; this site only reads it. Columns may change without notice —
see `schema-driven-design.mdc` and caretaker how-to `help_howto.php`.

## Stack

- PHP 8.1, plain (no framework), PDO prepared statements.
- MariaDB 11.x. `COLUMN_COMMENT` values are load-bearing (labels / EPICS PVs).
- No JS framework / build step. Shared CSS in `assets/style.css`.
  (Run/Group Info modals are CSS `:target` only.)
- Local test stack: `docker/` (MariaDB + Apache/PHP).

## File map (short)

```
includes/config.php              — Site knobs (no DB credentials, no layouts)
includes/dbconnect-template.php  — PDO template; tools/init_site.sh copies to a
                                   git-ignored local file. Prefer SELECT-only.
                                   Override with SITE_DB_* at deploy time.
includes/bootstrap.php           — config + dbconnect + schema + render_helpers
includes/schema.php              — INFORMATION_SCHEMA helpers only
includes/layouts/                — Caretaker presentation (touch these for UI)
  layout_{navbar,cards,tables,sections,run_summary,lookups,report}.php
includes/render_helpers.php      — Classify / group / render / require_* helpers
includes/descriptions_errors.php — Status-help catalog (help_errors.php)
includes/index_*.php             — Index filters / query / results
includes/report_*.php            — Report filters / query / results
index.php / detail_*.php         — Browse + detail pages
report.php / report_advanced.php — Filtered table + CSV
help_howto.php / help_errors.php — Caretaker how-to + status help
assets/style.css                 — All shared styling
docker/                          — Local test DB + web + seed
```

**Touch for presentation:** `includes/layouts/` only.  
**Do not put** real passwords, hosts, or production account names in the repo
or in these rules — use `SITE_DB_*` at deploy time.
